ns, texts or presentations about common technology. "}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to set up"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to get ready to do something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: I'm setting up this shot."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le03ob03aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about social activities."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "position"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " place; location"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: Can you show me how to position myself?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le03ob03aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "proper "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "correct"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Put your feet in the proper position."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le03ob03aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to align"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to line up; to put in the same direction "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You body will align itself the right way for the shot."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le03ob03aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "stride "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " step"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Stand two or three strides from the line."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le03ob03aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to lock "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to keep in position; to keep your joints (knee, elbow) straight "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Don't lock your knees."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le03ob03aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "loose"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "not tight; not locked"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Keep your knees loose."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le03ob03aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "master"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "expert"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You ought to take the master course."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le03ob03aud08"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Asking for Help"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " There are several ways to ask for help in English. You can use polite and casual language to do this. Let's look at one particular structure for asking for help."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use the structure<br/> Can/Could + you + show/tell + me + Question word"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Examples:</span><br/><span class=\"italic\">Can you show me how to position myself?<br/> Could you tell me where to stand?<br/> Can you tell me how the lessons work?<br/> Could you show me what I have to do?<br/> Can you tell me who that person is?</span>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":5,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Can/Could\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"you\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"show/tell\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"me\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Question word\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Could \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"you\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"tell\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"me \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">what</span> time it is, please?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Can\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"you\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"show\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"me \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">how</span> to use this?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Could \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"you\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"show\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"me \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">where</span> the washroom is?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Can\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"you\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"tell\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"me \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">when</span> the next train is?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can also use the structure<br/> Let me show/tell + you + question word"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Examples:</span><br/><span class=\"italic\">Let me show you how to stand.<br/> Let me show you where it is.<br/> Let me tell you what you should do.</span>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Giving Advice"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You use modals to give advice. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "The most common modals for giving advice are:<br/><span class=\"italic\"> should</span>, <span class=\"italic\">ought to</span> and <span class=\"italic\">had better</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can think of modals as \u201chelping verbs\u201d. They add meaning to the main verb of a sentence. In this case, these modals add the meaning of advice. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"> Should</span> is the most common modal used to give advice. <br/> <span class=\"italic\"> Ought to</span> and <span class=\"italic\"> had better</span>  are used for giving strong advice."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Subject\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Main Verb\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"should\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"put\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"your feet in the proper position.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"ought to \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"point\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"your feet in the right direction.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"had better not\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"step\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"on the line.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li>In conversation, it is common to use contractions with <span class=\"italic\"> had better</span>. </li></ul><span class=\"italic\">You'd better not step on the line.</span>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"typ